Week 3 Task 2

QuickBuild Solutions has multiple weaknesses in its current workflow
Requirements are verbally communicated meaning there is a huge risk of misunderstandings and details being 
left out and forgotten. A priority must have improvement would be to start using a digital backlog tool 
like Jira to record and track these requirements. This would be low cost and reduce the risk of missing requirements.

There is a lack of reviewing and testing code. This means that bugs, and bad sloppy code are being 
pushed straight to the main branch without any real testing or reviewing. Agile methods such as 
pair programming or utilising pull requests in github would catch these issues before they are commited.
This "Should" be a necessary improvement otherwise a sloppy final product would be released.

Due there being no changelogs or release notes, clients are unaware of any updates. This creates confusion 
and damages the trust between clients and QuickBuild. Agile models use sprint reviews and release documentation
as they go along. Automatic release notes "Could" enhance communication and increase professionalism.

Altogether these improvements are low cost steps toward a more lightweight process. They strengthen
QuickBuild's development practices without introducing heavy bureaucracy.

